acceptance criteria to satisfy:
  - THE contract SHALL cover inbound events, outbound sends, identities, conversations, threads, replies, mentions, commands, edits, deletion, reactions, attachments, voice, rich content, typing, receipts, rate limits, reconnect, cancellation, and capability discovery.
  - PLATFORM limitations SHALL be declared through capabilities and SHALL never be represented as successful unsupported behavior.
  - ADAPTER errors SHALL classify authentication, permission, malformed event, rate limit, transient network, permanent destination, unsupported feature, and uncertain acknowledgement.
  - EVERY adapter SHALL submit ordinary SessionActions through AgentConnection and SHALL NOT execute models, arbitrary tools, personal-memory reads, or alternate agent loops.
  - WEBHOOK adapters SHALL verify signatures before parsing untrusted bodies and socket or polling adapters SHALL persist bounded reconnect cursors.

[review page 3151-3300 of 3307]

  - A common conformance suite SHALL prove normalization, ordering, deduplication, media bounds, feature declarations, retries, cancellation, malformed input, restart, and isolation.
  - THE supported interactive matrix SHALL include Discord, Slack, Telegram, WhatsApp Cloud, Microsoft Teams, Google Chat, and Matrix.
  - EMAIL SHALL support inbound IMAP or provider events and outbound SMTP or provider send with threading, bounded attachments, reply identity, retry classification, and explicit possible-duplicate state.
  - EACH platform SHALL implement the subset it advertises for replies, threads, mentions, commands, edits, reactions, media, voice, typing, and receipts.
  - ACCOUNT setup SHALL expose required credentials, callback or webhook state, platform scopes, connection health, reconnect state, and a safe test action.
  - GROUP routes SHALL retain explicit mention, shared-memory, participant, tool, schedule, proactive-post, and profile isolation policies.
  - A real-account matrix SHALL prove inbound, reply, attachment, restart, scheduled return, rate limiting, duplicate handling, deletion or revocation, and cross-profile isolation for every platform called supported.

[review page 3301-3307 of 3307]

